WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.970
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.250
we wanted to find out the difference

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.600
between a US and a UK KFC.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.100
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.160
Now, you can't actually get
a small drink at a UK KFC.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.527
It starts at regular.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.490
This is what a regular drink looks like.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.090
Joe Avella: This is what
a US regular looks like.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.510
Harry: And this is what
a large drink looks like.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:29.171
Joe: And this is what
a US large looks like.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.453
Harry: This is a regular fries,

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:38.120
and this is a large fries.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.100
Joe: Here's the US regular. All right.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.610
And you want to go the next size up,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.968
this is the US large.

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.664
Googe!

00:00:47.664 --> 00:00:49.370
[laughing] Look at how big that is!

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.311
It's, like, five of
those ones that he had.

00:00:51.311 --> 00:00:52.870
Googe!

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.412
Harry: Let's find out
how much a large fries

00:00:54.412 --> 00:00:55.486
weighs in the UK.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.531
Joe: Let's weigh our large fry.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.412
Oh, man. Oh! [laughs]

00:01:08.412 --> 00:01:10.448
They're packed in there, dude!

00:01:10.448 --> 00:01:11.625
Look at that!

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:13.570
Is that everything?

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.460
Harry: This is what a regular
popcorn chicken looks like.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.562
Joe: We have a large popcorn chicken.

00:01:19.562 --> 00:01:22.120
Harry: And this is what a large
popcorn chicken looks like.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.120
Joe: And if you want to go
even larger than the large,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.700
you get yourself a popcorn chicken box.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.113
Something for you and
your buddies, I'm sure.

00:01:31.113 --> 00:01:32.963
You're not eating this by yourself.

00:01:33.884 --> 00:01:36.730
[nuggets plopping]

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.820
Did I lose any?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.760
No, no way!

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.910
Am I doing this without?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.440
Oh, don't jinx it.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.973
Yeah, aw, oh!

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.240
You, you,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.663
and you.

00:01:49.938 --> 00:01:50.771
That all of them?

00:01:50.771 --> 00:01:52.171
Producer: That's all.
Joe: Crumb.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:56.590
Harry: In the UK, you can
get buckets in three sizes.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.590
You can get a six piece,

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.006
you can get a 10 piece,

00:02:04.006 --> 00:02:05.758
or you can get a 14 piece.

00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:12.891
[laughs]

00:02:14.113 --> 00:02:15.671
Is it...? Ugh.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.261
Joe: Eight piece.

00:02:24.903 --> 00:02:26.015
Whoa!

00:02:26.015 --> 00:02:27.240
Ugh.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.254
12 piece.

00:02:28.254 --> 00:02:30.212
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:02:30.212 --> 00:02:32.615
This is, I'm not gonna
even, I can't even dump it.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:34.763
Yo!

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.371
Look how much chicken this is!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.500
Oh, my God, what a mess.

00:02:44.644 --> 00:02:46.253
Producer: I'm gonna get
the close-up cam now.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.010
Harry: Unfortunately, KFC in the UK

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.530
doesn't disclose its ingredients,

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.740
but what we do know is calories.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.273
For example, in the UK,

00:02:56.273 --> 00:02:59.590
a drum is 170 calories.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.248
Joe: And in the US,

00:03:01.248 --> 00:03:03.323
one of these guys for the original recipe

00:03:03.323 --> 00:03:04.838
is 130 calories.

00:03:04.838 --> 00:03:07.370
But if you get extra crispy,
like this guy right here,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.150
it's actually 170.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.560
Harry: USA is actually
still winning on calories.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.320
That's largely thanks to
the sides and the drinks.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.690
If you were to walk into a UK KFC

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.927
and order a three-piece meal

00:03:17.927 --> 00:03:20.800
and they gave you a
drum, a thigh, and a wing

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.230
with a large fries and a large Pepsi,

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.140
that would come to 1,155 calories.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.790
Joe: Our large fry is 930 calories,

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.231
and our large drink is 380.

00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:33.760
And if you were to order a three piece

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.950
with a large fry and a
large drink in the US,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.373
it would be roughly this many calories.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.080
The KFC in the US has
released its ingredients list.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.330
I would like to go over the
ingredients of the french fries

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.170
at the KFC in the US.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:48.830
All right, here we go.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.600
Sea salt, monosodium
glutamate, maltodextrin, salt,

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.920
dextrose, vegetable powders,
tricalcium phosphate,

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.250
hydrolyzed soy proteins,
spices, soybean oil,

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.433
natural flavors, potassium chloride,

00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:04.999
paprika extract (color),
turmeric extract (color),

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:07.050
potatoes (obviously), vegetable oil.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:11.870
It has soybean oil, canola,
cottonseed, and/or sunflower.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.303
Beached — "beached."

00:04:13.303 --> 00:04:14.670
Bleached wheat flour,

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.120
and it contains 2% or less
of rice flour, durum wheat,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.741
whoa, semolia?

00:04:20.741 --> 00:04:22.475
Sem-OH-lin-ah, sem-ol?

00:04:22.475 --> 00:04:23.309
Sem-OH-lin-ah.

00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:26.466
Durum wheat sem-OH-lia.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.457
Sem-oh-LIN-ah.

00:04:27.457 --> 00:04:28.470
I don't know what that word is.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.425
It looks like it's easy,
but it's hard to say.

00:04:30.425 --> 00:04:32.150
Sem-OH-lin-ah? Semolina?

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.170
Durum wheat semolina, there you go.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.250
Dextrin, salt, degermed yellow corn meal.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.660
Oh, thank God it's been degermed.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.340
Cornstarch, leavings
(sodium acid pyrophosphate,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.070
sodium bicarbonate), dextrose again,

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.650
xantham gum, there he is!

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.566
Annatto extract color,

00:04:48.566 --> 00:04:50.931
disodium dihydrox —

00:04:50.931 --> 00:04:55.090
disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate,

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:58.400
in parentheses, "to maintain color." OK.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.330
We add so many chemicals to our fries,

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.410
we add more chemicals to make it look like

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.810
it doesn't have any chemicals.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:09.135
Thank you, disodium dehydra, dehydra,

00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:10.660
what the f---?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.530
Yeah, whatever.

00:05:13.963 --> 00:05:15.730
Harry: Here are some things
you can only find on the menu

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.210
at a UK KFC.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.830
So, instead of a chicken sandwich,

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.700
what we call ours is the
chicken filet burger.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.410
I think it's pretty much the same thing.

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.090
It's, like, breaded and fried
chicken between two buns,

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.890
with some lettuce and some mayonnaise.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.260
We also have something
called the Zinger Burger,

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.090
which is pretty much the same thing,

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.200
but the spice level is
amped up a little bit.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.140
You can also turn these
burgers into a tower burger.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.250
What that does is adds
cheese and a hash brown

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.390
to the burger, which, in my opinion,

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.510
very worthwhile addition.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.750
Joe: We have some stuff in our
KFC they can't get in the UK.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.770
And, surprisingly, some
things I thought were, like,

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.350
kind of, like, paramount to the KFC menu.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:53.720
Mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.660
This to me seems like something

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.580
that has just always been part of KFC

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.830
along with the chicken.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.870
Look at those mashed potatoes, man.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.660
It's a tub of mashed potatoes.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.780
OK, let's make a mess.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.920
Oh, yeah!

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.334
Oh, my goodness, put that on the cover

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.495
of Gravy Aficionado Magazine!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.670
Another thing I didn't
realize you guys don't have,

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.820
biscuits, or, as you call them, scones.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.350
This is called the Famous Bowl.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:23.430
It is mashed potatoes and gravy and corn,

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.390
topped with popcorn
chicken, topped with cheese,

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:27.660
all in one bowl.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.940
Yeah, this thing, I don't think
I've ever had one of these,

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.900
'cause it looks ridiculous.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.230
Harry: Now, Joe, I'm glad you also think

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.680
that the Famous Bowl
doesn't look that great,

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.370
because, to me, that
looks like a nightmare.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.680
Now, we have a slightly different approach

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.170
to sides in the UK compared to the US.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.180
For example, our corn comes on the cob.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.110
Baked beans, these are slightly different

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.890
to the regular beans that you
might put on toast in the UK.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:51.740
They have kind of a barbecue
sauce flavor to them.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.100
There's a few other language differences,

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.450
like instead of chicken tenders,

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.730
we call ours chicken mini filets.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.140
Joe: Mini filets, chicken tenders,

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.430
they look exactly the same.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:00.650
We got those.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.900
Yes, they have corn, but
we have ours off the cob,

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.580
which I think is not
as good as on the cob.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.020
This pile right here, and, I know,

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:12.310
they do have wings at KFC
in the UK, yes, I know.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.951
But only in the US can
you order them by 48.

00:07:16.951 --> 00:07:18.620
[laughing]

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.520
48 wings!

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.260
I'm dying right now, man.
Producer: It sure smells good.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.570
Joe: They smell so good.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.370
The potpie, when I saw
a potpie on the menu,

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.210
I was like, "Yeah, a little side potpie."

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.220
No, dude. This thing
weighs, like, a puppy.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.656
This thing has kind of
got some weight to it.

00:07:33.656 --> 00:07:34.489
Harry: I gotta say,

00:07:34.489 --> 00:07:35.930
the potpie actually looks quite good.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.930
We love meat pies here in the UK.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.120
You'll often see people tucking into,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.700
like, a steak and kidney
pie or the chicken pie.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.150
But, yeah, they should probably put that

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:43.983
on the menu over here.

00:07:43.983 --> 00:07:45.640
I think they'd cash in
on the British market.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.130
Joe: Let's talk sauces. It's sauce talk.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.590
Sauce talk.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:52.930
I think that these
sauces are also specific

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.130
only to the US and not the UK.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:58.950
The KFC Finger Lookin'
Good Sauce, see that?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.183
We also have the
summertime barbecue sauce.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.890
Honey mustard.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.653
And, of course, buttermilk ranch.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:11.160
Harry: There are a few sauces
which are exclusive to the UK.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:14.610
For example, we have this
Spicy Supercharger dip,

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.530
which is kind of like a
spicy mayo-type thing.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.670
We have some sweet chili
sauce, garlic mayonnaise,

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.370
another really good option.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:25.480
Garlic mayo on chips is just fantastic.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.960
Joe: Why don't we have those sauces here?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.750
Oh, man, I want those.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.285
Harry: Now, usually, we'd have even more

00:08:31.285 --> 00:08:33.480
exclusive menu items to
show you, but unfortunately,

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.630
the UK KFCs are currently
operating with a reduced menu.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.260
Here's what you could
normally find on the menu

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:39.507
at a UK KFC.

00:08:39.507 --> 00:08:42.023
[typing]

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:50.000
A vegan burger, the Big Daddy burger,

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.230
a range of chicken wraps, some rice boxes,

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:58.300
onion rings, curry sauce, Krushems,

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.050
and a full range of hot drinks,

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.650
including English breakfast tea.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:06.260
Joe: In the UK, you can get teas,

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.570
including English breakfast tea.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:13.100
Now, technically you can't
get tea at the KFCs in the US,

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.190
but you can get something

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:18.040
called Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:21.070
which I think is probably pretty close.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:22.550
Harry: Yeah, that's pretty
much exactly the same

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.133
as a breakfast tea.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.003
Joe: Dude.

